.TH GIT-@-MAIN 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-main \- Switch to trunk branches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ main
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B git @ master
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B git @ root
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBmain\fR command switches to the trunk branch (typically 'main' or 'master') and pulls the latest changes. It provides a quick way to get back to the main development branch.
.PP
The \fBmaster\fR and \fBroot\fR commands are aliases for the \fBmain\fR command.
.PP
If you have uncommitted changes, the command will ask if you want to save them as WIP before switching.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH BEHAVIOR
.PP
The command follows this process:
.IP 1. 4
Determines the trunk branch:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Checks GitAT configuration (\fBat.trunk\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Falls back to \fBmain\fR if it exists
.IP \(bu 2
Falls back to \fBmaster\fR if \fBmain\fR doesn't exist
.IP \(bu 2
Shows error if neither exists
.RE
.IP 2. 4
Checks for uncommitted changes and offers to save to WIP
.IP 3. 4
Switches to the trunk branch if not already on it
.IP 4. 4
Pulls latest changes from remote (if origin exists)
.SH WIP FUNCTIONALITY
.PP
If uncommitted changes are detected, the command will prompt the user with:
.RS
.nf
? Save changes to WIP? (y/N)
.fi
.RE
.PP
If the user answers yes, the changes are saved using the GitAT WIP functionality:
.IP 1. 4
Stages all changes (\fBgit add -A\fR)
.IP 2. 4
Creates a commit with message \fB[WIP] <current-branch>\fR
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
To configure a specific trunk branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ _trunk develop
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Switch to trunk branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ main
.fi
.RE
.PP
Switch to trunk branch (alternative):
.RS
.nf
git @ master
git @ root
.fi
.RE
.SH SAFETY FEATURES
.PP
The command includes several safety features:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Validates that the trunk branch exists before switching
.IP \(bu 2
Checks for uncommitted changes and offers to save them
.IP \(bu 2
Shows informative messages about current status
.IP \(bu 2
Gracefully handles missing remote repositories
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-_trunk (1),
.BR git-@-wip (1),
.BR git (1)